{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1497878-intentionally-creating-chimerical-companions","id":1497878,"title":"Intentionally creating Chimerical Companions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-22T19:17:26-08:00","id":1497878,"title":"Intentionally creating Chimerical Companions","content":"So, I have either a really dumb or really smart question. We'll find out which one it is! I understand the mechanics of building a chimera as a chimerical companion, and I understand that spontaneous chimera may be created during Chrysalis or other special events. But *how* does a Changeling or Kinain intentionally create Chimerical companions, narrative-wise? Do they just say, &quot;I think I'll create an imaginary friend,&quot; or is there no rule about this, and it's up to the storyteller to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26676-squiggles","name":"Squiggles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-02T00:39:19-08:00","id":1498608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squiggles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1497878-intentionally-creating-chimerical-companions#post1497878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have either a really dumb or really smart question. We'll find out which one it is! I understand the mechanics of building a chimera as a chimerical companion, and I understand that spontaneous chimera may be created during Chrysalis or other special events. But *how* does a Changeling or Kinain intentionally create Chimerical companions, narrative-wise? Do they just say, &quot;I think I'll create an imaginary friend,&quot; or is there no rule about this, and it's up to the storyteller to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the fae actively create their chimerical companions (although certain Arts might allow for it). On the whole, they coalesce from dreams and emotions.<br /> <br /> Some chimerical companions will be imaginary friends from childhood. Others will be manifestations of a faerie's desires and wants. Others might materialise apparently out of thin air, with their significance a potential story hook for the characters.<br /> <br /> Some chimerical companions will also be chimera that arose independently of the kinain -- maybe the imaginary friend of a child who outgrew them, for instance, or the remnant of a particularly powerful/terrifying/enduring dream.<br /> <br /> In out-of-character terms, you're free to come up with an origin for them, provided the ST agrees. Or you can just ignore their origins and make the companion you want to have (perhaps returning to their origin story later on).<br /> <br /> I hope that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T23:48:56-08:00","id":1499034,"title":"","content":"I would say that usually they just find a chimera and recruit it. Dreamers make chimera all the time and without a source of glamour most of them vanish just as quickly. Give one a point of glamour to sustain it and then make some social rolls. Or whatever other rolls are thematically appropriate.<br /> <br /> Of course, people who dream in a freehold will make somewhat longer-lasting chimera because there is a source of glamour right there.<br /> <br /> If you want a custom one, Oneiromancy 2 lets you change a mortals dreams and Oneiromancy 4 lets you bring a chimera directly out of their dreams. Just be mindful of the effect messing with someone's dreams can have on the dreamer.<br /> <br /> What I miss is the rules from 2nd Ed where a mortal could essentially become poisoned with glamour and end up making chimera so powerful that they imprisoned the person who dreamed them into existence, using their powers to keep the person alive and asleep as much as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}